# Fixtures whose exact bytes are the thing under test.
#
# The AST byte-offset tests (test/sql/source_byte_offsets.test) assert that
# start_byte / end_byte slice the right bytes out of these files. If git
# normalized their line endings or re-encoded them, the fixtures would silently
# become LF/ASCII on a fresh clone and the tests would pass while testing
# nothing. `-text` means "never translate this file's line endings".
test/data/encoding/crlf_utf8.py -text
test/data/python/unicode.py -text
test/data/python/macros/patch_unicode.py -text

# The 26-language unparse corpus joined this list when byte-exact unparse
# landed (test/sql/ast_unparse_exact.test, tracker 047 "4b part 1"). That test
# pins LITERAL BYTE COUNTS and BYTE OFFSETS on these files -- 55 leaves / 172
# leaf bytes / 50 gap bytes for sample.py, and the hidden quote characters of
# sample.kt at bytes 75 and 78 -- so a checkout that rewrote their line endings
# would change every one of those numbers. It would fail loudly rather than
# silently, unlike the cases above, but it would fail for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the code under test. GitHub's checkout action happens not
# to translate today; `-text` makes that a guarantee instead of a default.
test/data/unparse_leaf_text/* -text

# The core-alone fixture and the file it indexes (M2 stage 3, tracker 057
# task 7). test/data/fixtures/core_alone_ast.csv is a committed AST carrying
# start_byte / end_byte for every node of test/data/python/sample_app.py, and
# test/sql/core_alone.test asserts that ast_unparse_exact_from reassembles that
# file BYTE FOR BYTE from the two together. A checkout that rewrote either
# file's line endings would move the offsets in one and the bytes in the other.
#
# Like the unparse corpus above, that fails LOUDLY -- MEASURED: shortening the
# fixture's root end_byte by one raised "'...sample_app.py' is now 4155 bytes
# but the parse covers 4154". So this is a guarantee replacing a default, not a
# fix for a silent-green hazard. sample_app.py is listed because the fixture
# made it byte-pinned; it was not before.
test/data/fixtures/core_alone_ast.csv -text
test/data/python/sample_app.py -text
